        <briefdescription>
<para>Select and budget theses from <computeroutput>profile</computeroutput> for a single discourse round. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Implements the §9.1 algorithm:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Filter <computeroutput>profile.typed_theses</computeroutput> to those whose <computeroutput>activation_rounds</computeroutput> list contains <computeroutput>round_number</computeroutput> (or have an empty list → all rounds active).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Sort survivors by <computeroutput>round_role_weights[round_role]</computeroutput> descending (unweighted theses receive weight 0.5 as neutral priority).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Greedily select theses in that order until <computeroutput>available_tokens</computeroutput> is exhausted, respecting each thesis&apos;s individual <computeroutput>token_budget</computeroutput> cap.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Non-selected theses (not in their activation round or budget exceeded) contribute a headline token: <computeroutput>"[{thesis_id}: {name}]"</computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para>Theses that have no <computeroutput>token_budget</computeroutput> (value -1) are treated as if they require <computeroutput>countTokens(description)</computeroutput> tokens — they never get an artificial cap but still consume budget.</para>
<para>When <computeroutput>profile</computeroutput> has no <computeroutput>typed_theses</computeroutput> the method returns an empty vector without error (backward compatible — caller falls back to plain string theses).</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>profile</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Philosophy profile whose theses to select. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>round_number</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Current discourse round (1–5). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>round_role</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><ref refid="namespacethemis_1_1prompt__engineering_1a2a4ac5e3cb74c8e141901185142cc45d" kindref="member">Role</ref> label for the round (e.g. &quot;PRO&quot;, &quot;REBUTTAL&quot;, &quot;SYNTHESIS&quot;). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>available_tokens</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Total token budget available for thesis injection. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>List of <computeroutput><ref refid="structthemis_1_1prompt__engineering_1_1_thesis_injection" kindref="compound">ThesisInjection</ref></computeroutput> entries (full + headline combined).</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Performance: ≤ 0.5 ms for ≤ 20 theses per profile. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
